  "qualifications": [
    "Only descriptor indices below the original 405-record bound, positive n = flags & 31 and members 0 <= member < n qualify. The zero-count clamp is not universally safe and supplies no reference.",
    "Original consumers request a logical 32-byte palette and select a 16-entry TLUT; flags bit 0x20 selects IA16 rather than RGBA16. This establishes static potential use, not invocation, rendering or historical allocation.",
    "Exactly 25 unchanged whole raw parents are covered. No mixed-parent splitting, zero-residual padding, whole-game closure or C/C++ credit follows."
  ],
